Understanding TTPs (Tactics, Techniques, and Procedures)

TTPs are known as the playbook of the adversary.

TTP stands for:

Tactics – the overall objective or goal of the attacker.

Techniques – the methods used to achieve the objective.

Procedures – the specific step-by-step actions followed.


TTPs help security teams:

Monitor indicators of compromise (IOCs).

Perform threat attribution and actor profiling.

Improve detection use cases.

Develop incident response and security playbooks.




