Quick Memory Trick

Think of the Cyber Kill Chain like a burglar breaking into a house:

1. Reconnaissance – Watching the house.


2. Weaponization – Preparing tools.


3. Delivery – Entering through a door/window.


4. Exploitation – Unlocking the door.


5. Installation – Hiding inside.


6. C2 – Calling the getaway driver.


7. Actions on Objectives – Stealing valuables.




---

One-Line Summary

> TTPs describe how attackers operate, while the Cyber Kill Chain describes the sequence of steps they follow during an attack.
